						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5133</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> There are no current reliable means of containing SCP-5133, currently it is contained in a 2 meter x 2 meter(7 ft x 7 ft) square room made of steel about 8&#160;cm (3 inch) thick inside of Site-██. Inside this room it is often stored on a pedestal in the center of the room, however it is often found in other places in the chamber. The chamber is to be kept cold, about 4 degrees Celsius (60°F) while SCP-5133 is inside. This is a privilege, and not a necessity. SCP-5133 can freely roam the Foundation with supervision of personnel with level 2 clearance or higher. If the object is seen outside of it’s chamber unsupervised, it is to be placed under supervision, or escorted to its containment chamber. Any resistance or misbehavior from SCP-5133 is to be noted, and the air conditioning in the objects cell is to be turned off until the next day as a form of punishment. If the object becomes hostile it is to be placed in a separate containment chamber that is under -6 degrees Celsius (30°F) for a minimum of 3 hours. SCP-5133 has the ability to leave it’s chamber at any point in time, making it difficult to contain, however it chooses to stay within the Foundation for the most part, giving it the classification of Euclid</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5133 appears to be a life size bust of King David from the Hebrew Bible. The object is about 63&#160;cm tall (25 in) and about 40&#160;cm wide (16 in). Close research on the object has determined that it is made of a mixture of 43% porcelain 37% terracotta, and 19% concrete, and 1% uranium. SCP-5133 is sentient, and is capable of speech in languages such as English, French, Hebrew, and Greek. Despite having any muscles or muscle like structure in the bust, it’s face remains very animated when speaking, or reacting to situations. It believes itself to be more intelligent than everybody else, often referring to personnel as “Pleb” or “Infidel” with the exception of Dr. ███████ Ashe, who it refers to as “Sir”. The object has shown the ability to telepathy, as well as affect living organisms mentally. SCP-5133 is capable of mind reading, forcing thoughts upon others, and killing via anomalous, telepathic means. The process of said killing, as described by victims of SCP-5133, includes a faint ringing sound that gets louder over the course of 5 or so days, eventually causing the subject's eardrums to burst, followed by death seconds after. Personnel have been able to survive this, however with major hearing damage. Most instances of survival happen due to SCP-5133 being told to stop, or threatened. Any surviving victims are to be given an immediate psychiatric evaluation and treated accordingly. The object has been known to move via rolling on the floor, sliding, or even levitating, although this method of travel is the least common. SCP-5133 is often cooperative with staff and often has “enjoyable” conversations with them, as described by Officer ██████.</p> <p><strong>Addendum 5133:1 Discovery:</strong> SCP-5133 was originally on display at the ██████ Museum in █████ ███, Jerusalem. The first anomalous sighting of the object was on ██/██/████ at 4:30&#160;pm. It was reported as stolen to the authorities despite having no evidence of a break in, or of the cabinet it was in being disturbed in any way. Stationed operatives from <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#iota-10" target="_blank">Mobile Task Force Iota-10</a> had investigated and found SCP-5133 inside an abandoned building nearby, sitting on a cinder block. SCP-5133 was taken into custody with no resistance from the object. It wasn’t until it was put into containment that researchers had discovered it’s ability to think and speak.</p> <p><strong>Addendum 5133:2 Test Logs:</strong></p> <blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test A - 07/16/2020</strong></span><br /> <strong>Conducted by</strong><br /> Dr. J. Ashe<br /> <strong>Subject:</strong><br /> SCP-5133<br /> <strong>Procedure:</strong><br /> SCP-5133 will be presented with a 54 page math assignment, all having to do with overly elaborate equations. It will be timed and and it's score will be documented.<br /> <strong>Results:</strong><br /> After about 140 seconds had passed, SCP-5133 had finished the entire assignment with a perfect score. All 547 questions had a perfect answer with no sign of cheating, or manipulation to the assignment.<br /> <strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br /> SCP-5133 appeared to have no struggle during the assignment and even seemed insulted that we had believed it would have any struggle at all. The object appears to excel in mathematic problem solving.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test B - 07/24/2020</strong></span><br /> <strong>Conducted by</strong><br /> Dr. R. Farlow<br /> <strong>Subject:</strong><br /> SCP-5133<br /> <strong>Procedure:</strong><br /> SCP-5133 will be asked to end world hunger, it's reactions and response will be documented and covered in an interview.<br /> <strong>Results:</strong><br /> After the question was asked, SCP-5133 had said “I would not be able to do that on my own, however, using your primitive, yet still effective technology, I’m sure killing off enough people to make that happen is quite possible.”<br /> <strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br /> According to SCP-5133, decreasing the human population drastically would be the most effective way of ending world hunger. It appears that it did not take morals into account when making this statement.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test C - 08/07/2020</strong></span><br /> <strong>Conducted by</strong><br /> Dr. J. Ashe<br /> <strong>Subject:</strong><br /> SCP-5133<br /> <strong>Procedure:</strong><br /