in general into consideration. Killing her isn't curing her.<br /> <strong>SCP-5133:</strong> She no longer has cancer. Does she?<br /> <strong>Dr. Farlow:</strong> What the hell? [Dr. Farlow began to raise his voice] You think killing a person is making them better? She could have been cured, she could have lived, but you killed her! Why?<br /> <strong>SCP-5133:</strong> [SCP-5133 began to grow frustrated] There is no reason to shout. You asked me to get rid of her cancer, and did I not deliver?<br /> <strong>Dr. Farlow:</strong> You think you did something good? Tell me something. If you're so smart, why didn't you take ethical treatment into consideration?<br /> <strong>SCP-5133:</strong> [SCP-5133 began raising it's voice] Do NOT insult my intelligence, you idiotic fool. I'm the one who got rid of her cancer, if I had the moral high ground in that situation, she would have died of her cancer sooner than it would have been cured<br /> <strong>Dr. Farlow:</strong> Are you sure? Many people have survived cancer, why wouldn't she. I think you just wanted an excuse to kill. You're a mindless killing machine.<br /> <strong>Dr. Ashe:</strong> [From outside the room] Dr. Farlow don't provoke the SCP<br /> [SCP-5133 raised a pencil in the room and brutally murdered Dr. Farlow]<br /> <strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> Dr. Ashe had rushed into the room afterwards and took SCP-5133 to it's freezer room and Dr. Farlow's body was taken to the lab for a biopsy. This incident will further be recognized as Incident:5133-F</p> <p><strong>An Interview Conducted by Doctor J. Ashe</strong></p> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5133</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> This interview was a confrontation after the aftermath of Incident:5133-F</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong><br /> <strong>Dr. Ashe:</strong> What the hell happened in there with Dr. Farlow?<br /> <strong>SCP-5133:</strong> Sir, you told him you